<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 394-400: rhinoceros and allied skulls by coordinate-grid transformation (Osborn) (Hyrachyus agrarius, Aceratherium tridactylum, Titanotherium, tapir, horse, rabbit (diagrammatic skulls after Osborn; Thompson pp. 760-764))",
        "Thompson (1917) Figs. 394-400: rhinoceros and allied skulls by coordinate-grid transformation (Osborn) faithfully reproduces Hyrachyus agrarius, Aceratherium tridactylum, Titanotherium, tapir, horse, rabbit (diagrammatic skulls after Osborn; Thompson pp. 760-764) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-055-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-055-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-055-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-055-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-055_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Hyrachyus agrarius, Aceratherium tridactylum, Titanotherium, tapir, horse, rabbit (diagrammatic skulls after Osborn; Thompson pp. 760-764) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-055_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py> ;
    schema:about "Hyrachyus agrarius, Aceratherium tridactylum, Titanotherium, tapir, horse, rabbit (diagrammatic skulls after Osborn; Thompson pp. 760-764)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: that Ceratotherium segmentation quantifies the Osborn diagram fit",
        "does_not_claim: that TPS strictly dominates affine on the primary pair (it does not on Procrustes or IoU)",
        "does_not_claim: that modern 3D GM datasets validate the rabbit/horse panels (Leporidae cache mismatch)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Ceratotherium photograph bone/matrix mask (descriptive, excluded from verdict statistics)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: IoU, Pearson r, RMSE/cs, chamfer/cs, Procrustes; primary-only parameter sweep; E1 Jacobian check",
        "reconstructed_in_script: phi as TPS on automatically matched grid peaks; identity, affine, and shuffled-grid controls",
        "reported_in_source: Fig. 394 Hyrachyus skull with rectangular Cartesian grid; Fig. 395 Aceratherium in a deformed grid (p. 760-761)",
        "reported_in_source: extensions to Titanotherium, tapir, horse, and rabbit by the same method (Figs. 397-400, pp. 763-764)",
        "reported_in_source: methodological claim that allied skulls differ by smooth coordinate transformation of a common diagram",
        "reported_in_source: occipital Aceratherium variants related by conformal transformations (Fig. 396, p. 762)",
        "transfer_boundary: affine beating TPS on Procrustes and IoU means the registered non-affine spline claim is only partially supported for Aceratherium",
        "transfer_boundary: automatic NN grid matching still approximates Thompson's hand correspondences" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-055_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py; output: docs/media/t1917_055_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png; organism: Hyrachyus agrarius, Aceratherium tridactylum, Titanotherium, tapir, horse, rabbit (diagrammatic skulls after Osborn; Thompson pp. 760-764); environment: python 3.12, numpy 1.26.4, scipy 1.x (pip, requirements.txt lower bound >=1.7), scikit-image >=0.19, matplotlib >=3.3, Pillow >=8.0, lean 4.35.0 (elan stable); claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Fig. 394 Hyrachyus skull with rectangular Cartesian grid; Fig. 395 Aceratherium in a deformed grid (p. 760-761) | occipital Aceratherium variants related by conformal transformations (Fig. 396, p. 762) | extensions to Titanotherium, tapir, horse, and rabbit by the same method (Figs. 397-400, pp. 763-764) | methodological claim that allied skulls differ by smooth coordinate transformation of a common diagram; reconstructed_in_script: phi as TPS on automatically matched grid peaks; identity, affine, and shuffled-grid controls | IoU, Pearson r, RMSE/cs, chamfer/cs, Procrustes; primary-only parameter sweep; E1 Jacobian check | Ceratotherium photograph bone/matrix mask (descriptive, excluded from verdict statistics); transfer_boundary: automatic NN grid matching still approximates Thompson's hand correspondences | affine beating TPS on Procrustes and IoU means the registered non-affine spline claim is only partially supported for Aceratherium; does_not_claim: that TPS strictly dominates affine on the primary pair (it does not on Procrustes or IoU) | that modern 3D GM datasets validate the rabbit/horse panels (Leporidae cache mismatch) | that Ceratotherium segmentation quantifies the Osborn diagram fit]; other sources: On Growth and Form (Ch. XVII, On the Theory of Transformations, pp. 760-764, Figs. 394-400, skulls after Osborn) <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>, The Extinct Rhinoceroses of North America <https://archive.org/details/extinctrhinocero01osbo>, Modern Leporidae skull GM cache (portfolio JSON) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/portfolio/results/leporidae_skulls.json>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.24792> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-055-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-055-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-055-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-055-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-055-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-055-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-055-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-055-4> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "geometric — Thompson (1917) method of transformations applied to Osborn rhinoceros-allied skull diagrams (Figs. 394-400)" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 8.21e-01 .

