<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 394-400: rhinoceros and allied skulls by coordinate-grid transformation (Osborn) — Model fidelity to source: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "E2/E6, E4, E5 and E7 implemented as stated; eight Lean theorems compile with 0 sorry; Pass 2 adds numerical E1 via jacobian_min_det/check_no_fold on the primary TPS (min det inside skull 0.259 over 21 stages). Remaining deductions: Fig. 394-395 grid ink not digitised line-by-line; affine map fits the primary outline slightly better than the TPS on Procrustes, so the strict \"smooth non-affine grid\" reading is not numerically dominant." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
